  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# 02 - End-to-End Walkthrough\\n",
        "\\n",
        "This notebook explains how data flows through **SafetyOps Copilot** from ingestion to dashboard, and how to run the system locally."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. Architecture recap\\n",
        "\\n",
        "Components:\\n",
        "\\n",
        "- **FastAPI API** (`apps/api`)\\n",
        "  - Ingests events (`/events/text`, `/events/vision`).\\n",
        "  - Exposes `/health`, `/metrics`, `/events/recent`, `/aggregates/summary`.\\n",
        "- **Worker service** (`services/worker`)\\n",
        "  - Consumes events from Redis Streams.\\n",
        "  - Runs text and vision inference.\\n",
        "  - Writes raw and enriched events plus daily aggregates to Postgres.\\n",
        "- **Streamlit UI** (`apps/ui`)\\n",
        "  - Produces demo events.\\n",
        "  - Displays live enriched events and aggregates.\\n",
        "- **Infra** (`infra/`)\\n",
        "  - Postgres, Redis, MLflow, Prometheus, Grafana via Docker Compose.\\n",
        "- **Shared library** (`safetyops/`)\\n",
        "  - Settings, logging, domain models, ML wrappers, streaming, DB, metrics."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 1.1 Event types\\n",
        "\\n",
        "We focus on two event types:\\n",
        "\\n",
        "- `text_event` – incident text with optional metadata.\\n",
        "- `vision_event` – image path or upload representing a scene for PPE checks.\\n",
        "\\n",
        "Both are wrapped in a normalized `EventEnvelope` with fields like `id`, `created_at`, `correlation_id`, and `source`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Running the system locally\\n",
        "\\n",
        "### 2.1 Start infra\\n",
        "\\n",
        "From the repo root:\\n",
        "\\n",
        "```bash\\n",
        "make up\\n",
        "```\\n",
        "\\n",
        "This brings up Postgres, Redis, MLflow, Prometheus, and Grafana as defined in `infra/docker-compose.local.yml`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 2.2 Start services\\n",
        "\\n",
        "In three separate terminals (with your Python virtualenv activated):\\n",
        "\\n",
        "```bash\\n",
        "# Terminal 1: API\\n",
        "uvicorn apps.api.main:app --reload --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\\n",
        "\\n",
        "# Terminal 2: Worker\\n",
        "python -m services.worker.run\\n",
        "\\n",
        "# Terminal 3: Streamlit UI\\n",
        "streamlit run apps/ui/main.py --server.port 8501\\n",
        "```\\n",
        "\\n",
        "You should then be able to access:\\n",
        "\\n",
        "- API docs: `http://localhost:8000/docs`\\n",
        "- UI: `http://localhost:8501`\\n",
        "- Prometheus: `http://localhost:9090`\\n",
        "- MLflow: `http://localhost:5000`\\n",
        "- Grafana: `http://localhost:3000` (default admin/admin)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Event flow walkthrough\\n",
        "\\n",
        "### 3.1 Text incident flow\\n",
        "\\n",
        "1. An operator enters an incident description in the Streamlit **Incident Triage** tab or via API:\\n",
        "\\n",
        "   ```bash\\n",
        "   curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/events/text \\\\n",
        "        -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\\n",
        "        -d '{\"text\": \"Worker slipped on wet floor\", \"metadata\": {\"site\": \"A\"}}'\\n",
        "   ```\\n",
        "\\n",
        "2. FastAPI validates the payload and wraps it into an `EventEnvelope`.\\n",
        "3. The envelope is published to Redis Streams using `RedisStreamsEventBus`.\\n",
        "4. The worker reads from the stream, stores the raw event, runs `classify_incident`,\\n",
        "   stores the enriched event and updates daily aggregates.\\n",
        "5. The UI queries `/events/recent` and `/aggregates/summary` to show triage results and trends."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 3.2 Vision PPE flow\\n",
        "\\n",
        "1. A vision event is produced either via:\\n",
        "   - `POST /events/vision` with an `image_path` pointing to a local sample; or\\n",
        "   - File upload from the UI (saved into `data/uploads/`).\\n",
        "2. FastAPI wraps the payload in an `EventEnvelope` with type `vision_event` and publishes it to the stream.\\n",
        "3. The worker consumes the event and calls `run_ppe_inference` from `safetyops.ml.vision.yolo`.\\n",
        "4. The inference wrapper computes a simple PPE compliance heuristic and returns a `VisionPPEDetection`.\\n",
        "5. The worker stores the enriched event and updates aggregates, mapping compliance scores to severity buckets.\\n",
        "6. The UI displays compliance-related information in the Live Feed and Ops Dashboard tabs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Interpreting outputs\\n",
        "\\n",
        "### 4.1 Enriched events\\n",
        "\\n",
        "Enriched events are stored in the `enriched_events` table and exposed via `/events/recent`. A typical response item contains:\\n",
        "\\n",
        "- `id` – event id.\\n",
        "- `event_type` – `text_event` or `vision_event`.\\n",
        "- `created_at` – timestamp.\\n",
        "- `correlation_id` – for tracing across services.\\n",
        "- `category` – category label for text events or a synthetic label for vision events.\\n",
        "- `severity` – interpreted severity (low/medium/high).\\n",
        "- `enrichment` – JSON payload with model-specific details (e.g., compliance_score).\\n",
        "\\n",
        "These are visualized in the Streamlit **Live Feed** and **Incident Triage** tabs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### 4.2 Aggregates\\n",
        "\\n",
        "The worker maintains a `daily_aggregates` table keyed by `(date, event_type, severity)` with a `count` field.\\n",
        "\\n",
        "- `/aggregates/summary` aggregates counts over a recent day window.\\n",
        "- The Streamlit **Ops Dashboard** tab uses this to plot counts by event type and severity.\\n",
        "\\n",
        "This supports quick operational questions such as:\\n",
        "\\n",
        "- Are high-severity incidents trending up or down?\\n",
        "- Which sites or event types are driving the most risk (once we add site metadata)?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5. Extending the system\\n",
        "\\n",
        "Future iterations (documented in `context/05_ROADMAP.md`) may include:\\n",
        "\\n",
        "- Upgrading the rule-based classifier to a learned model.\\n",
        "- Fine-tuning the YOLO PPE model on custom data.\\n",
        "- Adding monitoring views for model drift and performance.\\n",
        "- Integrating with alerting channels (Slack, email, ticketing).\\n",
        "\\n",
        "When making such changes, update the context files and this notebook to keep the end-to-end story consistent."
      ]
    },
